  'Teacher education students benefit from considering how people learn, develop and respond to different situations. Laboratory-based work can encourage careful observation, reflective thinking and a more informed understanding of individual differences in educational settings.',
  'Under faculty guidance, practical activities may help students examine concepts, discuss examples and interpret learning experiences responsibly. The emphasis is on using evidence thoughtfully, asking clear questions and recognising that learners bring varied needs and perspectives to the classroom.',
